I've had my best game yet so far with Carter (yeah, real original, I
know...) the gnomish archaeologist.  Got down to Minetown at level 1
to donate, had to level to survive, but managed to donate twice more. 
He's down to level 10 with very nice armor (including some +2
gauntlets of power), a +4 pickaxe, and a ring of slow digestion, and
got the amulet from Sokoban.  He's solid.  The only problem is... I
have no experience with the midgame for a roguish character.

I've noticed that archaeologists get awfully short-changed when it
comes to hit points, and don't do so well in melee unless you get one
heck of an artifact weapon, or a heavily enchanted pickaxe of mattock.
 What's the smart way to progress with the delvers?  I'm reluctant to
abandon the pick-axe for anything other than an artifact weapon, and
no opportunities have come by.  His HP, while pretty steady and
well-protected with -15 AC, makes me way about any potentially
powerful creature.  And his spell points are... surprisingly high. 
Should I start reading spellbooks and looking for nonmetallic armor,
or should I stay heavily armored and just ignore the steadily rising
amount of spell power?

